<title>UK: Wheat ship repairs underway at Port Weller, Canada.</title>
<headline>Wheat ship repairs underway at Port Weller, Canada.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada-flagged wheat carrier Canadian Mariner is at Port Weller undergoing repairs to its bow, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Repairs to the 27,350 dwt vessel were expected to take five weeks.</p>
<p>The bulker was carrying 25,000 tonnes of wheat from Thunder Bay, Ontario, to Quebec City, when it ran aground on the St. Lawrence seaway on June 18, and subsequently refloated on June 22.</p>
